.Dd 2026-05-30
.Dt NOMAD-REINSTALL 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nomad-reinstall
.Nd wipe all state and reinstall from scratch
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm nomad reinstall
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm nomad reinstall
performs a full wipe followed by a fresh install in one step. It asks for a
single confirmation up front, then proceeds without further prompts.
.Pp
The wipe stops and removes all NOMAD containers and named volumes, removes the
Ollama LaunchAgent and its plist, removes the secrets file, removes all data on
the data drive (databases, Ollama models, stored content), and removes the
cached compose images so the install pulls fresh. Homebrew tools (Ollama,
OrbStack,
.Xr jq 1 )
and this command bundle stay intact.
.Pp
After the wipe it re-runs
.Ic nomad install
against the same data root, so you are not prompted to choose a drive again.
Reach for this when an install is corrupted beyond what a plain
.Ic nomad install
repair can fix and you want a clean slate without running the wipe and install
steps by hand.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic nomad reinstall
Confirm once, then wipe everything and reinstall onto the same data drive.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nomad 1 ,
.Xr nomad-install 1 ,
.Xr nomad-uninstall 1
